CONFIG_MACHINE_NAME
  The name shown in BIOS identification strings.

CONFIG_BIOS_BRAND
  Short brand name shown on the POST banner.

CONFIG_BIOS_STYLE_NAME
  Style name shown in the POST banner subtitle.

CONFIG_WEBSITE
  Website URL shown on the POST screen.

CONFIG_ROS_RELEASE
  ROS firmware release number (0-255).

CONFIG_ROS_ISSUE
  ROS firmware issue number (0-255).

CONFIG_BASE_MEMORY_KB
  Amount of conventional base memory in kilobytes.
  The PC1640 originally shipped with 640 KB, but some boards
  may have 608 KB (reserving top 32 KB for EMS).

CONFIG_HAS_MATH_COPROCESSOR
  Report that an 8087 math coprocessor is installed.

CONFIG_COM1_BASE
  I/O base address for COM1 serial port.
  Standard value: 0x03F8.

CONFIG_COM2_BASE
  I/O base address for COM2 serial port.
  Standard value: 0x02F8.

CONFIG_LPT1_BASE
  I/O base address for LPT1 parallel port.
  Standard value: 0x0378.

CONFIG_LPT2_BASE
  I/O base address for LPT2 parallel port.
  Standard value: 0x03BC.

CONFIG_VIDEO_80X25_COLOR
  Use 80x25 color text as the default video equipment setting.

CONFIG_VIDEO_40X25_COLOR
  Use 40x25 color text as the default video equipment setting.

CONFIG_VIDEO_EGA_ADAPTER
  Use EGA adapter as the default video equipment setting.

CONFIG_VIDEO_MONO
  Use monochrome as the default video equipment setting.

CONFIG_VIDEO_ATTRIBUTE
  Default text attribute byte for POST display (hex).
  0x07 = normal white-on-black.

CONFIG_VIDEO_PEGA_STANDALONE_ROM
  Build the separate 32 KiB PEGA video ROM image for the normal PC1640
  C000h socket. Use this when you want the motherboard ROS to behave like a
  stock machine with a distinct video BIOS image.

CONFIG_VIDEO_PEGA_INROM_DRIVER
  Build the minimal PEGA text-mode INT 10h path directly into the 16 KiB ROS
  instead of relying on a separate C000h video ROM. This is mainly for
  constrained ROM experiments; stock-compatible setups normally leave it off.

CONFIG_VIDEO_DIRECT_TEXT_INIT
  Perform direct text mode initialization before the PEGA option ROM
  is called. Required for correct display on PC1640 hardware.

CONFIG_VIDEO_USE_PC1640_SWITCH_BLOCK
  Read the PC1640 switch block to determine display configuration.

CONFIG_VIDEO_QUERY_ROM_STATE
  Query the video ROM for its current state after initialization.

CONFIG_VIDEO_FIXUP_FROM_SWITCH_BLOCK
  Apply video state fixups based on the PC1640 switch block settings.

CONFIG_VIDEO_OPTION_ROM_SCAN_ENABLED
  Scan for and execute video option ROMs in the C000-C7FF range.

CONFIG_OPTION_ROM_SCAN_ENABLED
  Scan for and execute non-video option ROMs in the C800-EFFF range.

CONFIG_HAS_FLOPPY_CONTROLLER
  Enable support for the onboard floppy disk controller.
  Disable this if no floppy controller is present and you want
  to boot exclusively from IDE.

CONFIG_FLOPPY_SUPPORT_35DD
  Enable support for 720K 3.5-inch DD floppy drives.
  If disabled, only 360K 5.25-inch DD drives are supported.

CONFIG_FLOPPY_A_NONE
  Drive A is not installed.

CONFIG_FLOPPY_A_180K
  Drive A is a 180K 5.25" single-sided DD floppy drive.

CONFIG_FLOPPY_A_360K
  Drive A is a 360K 5.25" DD floppy drive.

CONFIG_FLOPPY_A_720K
  Drive A is a 720K 3.5" DD floppy drive.

CONFIG_FLOPPY_B_NONE
  Drive B is not installed.

CONFIG_FLOPPY_B_180K
  Drive B is a 180K 5.25" single-sided DD floppy drive.

CONFIG_FLOPPY_B_360K
  Drive B is a 360K 5.25" DD floppy drive.

CONFIG_FLOPPY_B_720K
  Drive B is a 720K 3.5" DD floppy drive.

CONFIG_FLOPPY_ENABLE_AH08_COMPAT
  Enable the INT 13h AH=08h (get drive parameters) compatibility
  path. Required by some DOS versions.

CONFIG_EMS_ENABLED
  Enable the built-in LIM EMS 3.2 driver for the Lo-tech 2MB EMS
  Board (or compatible). Provides INT 67h expanded memory services
  with 128 pages (2 MiB) through a 64 KiB page frame.
  On the PC1640DD profile this is a deliberate non-stock exception.

CONFIG_EMS_IO_BASE
  Base I/O address for the Lo-tech EMS board page registers.
  The four consecutive ports (base+0..base+3) each control one
  16 KiB window in the page frame. Default: 0x0260.

CONFIG_EMS_FRAME_SEGMENT
  Segment address of the 64 KiB EMS page frame. Must not overlap
  with video memory, option ROMs, or the system BIOS area.
  Default: 0xD000 (physical D0000-DFFFF).

CONFIG_SERIAL_INT14_ENABLED
  Provide BIOS INT 14h RS-232 services. Disabling removes src/serial.c
  from the link (~400 bytes) and frees ROS space for other features.

CONFIG_PRINTER_ENABLED
  Provide INT 17h printer, IRQ7, and INT 05h print-screen handling.
  Disabling removes src/printer.c from the link (~800 bytes).

CONFIG_XTIDE_ENABLED
  Build the XTIDE Universal BIOS for 8-bit ISA IDE. Produces
  build/ide_xtl.bin for the C800 option-ROM window using the upstream
  XT Large module set. The motherboard ROS stays separate unless you
  also enable CONFIG_XTIDE_EMBEDDED_IN_ROS.

CONFIG_XTIDE_EMBEDDED_IN_ROS
  Pack zlib-compressed XTIDE into the 16 KiB motherboard ROM image with
  a small decompressor. The embedded exception uses build/ide_tiny.bin
  internally because larger XTIDE profiles do not fit the PC1640DD ROS.
  Prefer the external ide_xt.bin default unless you have trimmed other
  features and verified a larger profile in your emulator or target.

CONFIG_XTIDE_BASE
  I/O base address for the XTIDE IDE controller.
  Common values: 0x0300, 0x0320, 0x0340.

CONFIG_XTIDE_FULL_MODE
  Enable XTIDE full mode. This allows XTIDE to steal a small amount
  of base RAM for runtime data structures and enables features such
  as EDD and compatible DPT tables. PC1640DD external XTIDE builds are
  currently forced to lite mode because 86Box's PC/XT XTIDE path can
  hang in BSY polling with the advanced/full-mode profile.

CONFIG_XTIDE_STEAL_SIZE
  Number of KiB of conventional memory XTIDE may reserve in full
  mode. The stock XTIDE default is 1 KiB.

XTIDE profile notes
  PC1640DD external builds default to the smaller ide_xt.bin profile
  (8 KiB, lite mode, no EDD/compatible-table extras) because it is the
  profile that currently boots reliably in 86Box. The tree still also
  emits ide_xtl.bin as a larger alternate build artifact. Embedded XTIDE
  builds are fixed to the upstream XT Tiny profile so the motherboard ROS
  can still carry and relocate it.

CONFIG_XTIDE_BOOT_DISPLAY_MODE
  Raw XTIDE display mode byte used by the option ROM before its boot
  menu or hotkey UI runs. Common values: 0x04 (default text), 0x07
  (mono), 0x02 or 0x03 (80-column CGA).

CONFIG_XTIDE_BOOT_TIMEOUT_TICKS
  XTIDE boot-menu timeout in BIOS timer ticks (18.2 Hz).

CONFIG_XTIDE_BOOT_DRIVE
  XTIDE default boot drive number, typically 0x80 for the first hard
  disk.

CONFIG_XTIDE_MIN_FLOPPY_COUNT
  Minimum floppy count reported by XTIDE's boot helpers.

CONFIG_XTIDE_CLEAR_BDA_HD_COUNT
  Clear the BIOS Data Area hard-disk count before XTIDE drive
  detection. Some machines require this, but it is not the default.

CONFIG_XTIDE_SERIAL_SCAN_DETECT
  Allow XTIDE serial scan detect, including the ALT-key trigger used
  by upstream XTIDE.

CONFIG_XTIDE_IDLE_TIMEOUT
  Raw XTIDE standby timeout byte. Zero disables it; other values use
  XTIDE's native encoding.

CONFIG_XTIDE_EDD_MAX_SECTORS
  Maximum sectors per XTIDE EDD request. Upstream XTIDE defaults to
  127 sectors.

CONFIG_XTIDE_TIMEOUT_DRQ / CONFIG_XTIDE_TIMEOUT_BSY / CONFIG_XTIDE_TIMEOUT_DRDY
  Raw XTIDE polling timeout values in BIOS timer ticks. These replace
  the old custom-driver poll-loop tuning with XTIDE-native timings.

CONFIG_XTIDE_MASTER_* / CONFIG_XTIDE_SLAVE_*
  Per-drive XTIDE settings for probe enable, block mode, translation
  mode, write-cache policy, forced CHS geometry, and forced LBA cap.
  Translation mode encoding is 0=normal, 1=large, 2=assisted-LBA,
  3=auto. Write-cache encoding is 0=default, 1=disable, 2=enable.

CONFIG_HD_BOOT_ENABLED
  Enable the INT 19h hard-disk boot attempt for drive 80h after any
  floppy boot attempts. When CONFIG_XTIDE_ENABLED is set, hard-disk
  boot is always compiled in. When the onboard floppy controller is
  disabled or both drives are "Not installed", hard-disk boot is
  enabled automatically even if this option is off (there is no
  other boot device). The BIOS does not require BDA drive count to
  be non-zero before trying 80h so XTIDE can answer INT 13h first.

CONFIG_UART_INIT
  UART initialization byte written during serial port setup.
  0xE3 = 9600 baud, 8N1.

CONFIG_RTC_DEFAULT_SECONDS
  Default RTC seconds value used when battery is dead (0-59).

CONFIG_RTC_DEFAULT_MINUTES
  Default RTC minutes value used when battery is dead (0-59).

CONFIG_RTC_DEFAULT_HOURS
  Default RTC hours value used when battery is dead (0-23).

CONFIG_RTC_DEFAULT_DAY_OF_MONTH
  Default RTC day of month used when battery is dead (1-31).

CONFIG_RTC_DEFAULT_MONTH
  Default RTC month used when battery is dead (1-12).

CONFIG_RTC_DEFAULT_YEAR
  Default RTC 2-digit year used when battery is dead (0-99).

CONFIG_RTC_DEFAULT_CENTURY
  Default RTC century used when battery is dead (19 or 20).

CONFIG_POST_SYSTEM_STATUS_TEST_ENABLED
  Exercise the PC1640 motherboard status latch path during POST. This checks
  the machine-specific ports used for board status, video strap reporting,
  and related ROS diagnostics.

CONFIG_POST_RTC_TEST_ENABLED
  Exercise RTC and NVR access during POST. Keep this enabled for fidelity if
  you expect the MC146818-compatible clock and the PC1640 NVR defaults to
  match the original firmware path.

CONFIG_POST_KEYBOARD_TEST_ENABLED
  Run the late-POST keyboard BAT check and clear the BIOS keyboard buffer
  before handing control to DOS.

CONFIG_POST_MOUSE_TEST_ENABLED
  Probe the PC1640 motherboard mouse interface during POST. This tests the
  port path only; it does not require a mouse to be actively used at boot.

CONFIG_MODE_ELKS
  Switch the BIOS into the alternate ELKS-oriented operating mode. Normal
  PC1640-compatible DOS and POST behavior should leave this disabled.

CONFIG_PC1640_NVR_ENTER_TOKEN
  Default Amstrad PC1640 NVR token returned for the Enter key.
  Format: scan-code in the high byte, ASCII code in the low byte.

CONFIG_PC1640_NVR_DELETE_TOKEN
  Default Amstrad PC1640 NVR token returned for the Delete key.
  Format: scan-code in the high byte, ASCII code in the low byte.

CONFIG_PC1640_NVR_JOYSTICK1_TOKEN
  Default Amstrad PC1640 NVR token assigned to joystick button 1.

CONFIG_PC1640_NVR_JOYSTICK2_TOKEN
  Default Amstrad PC1640 NVR token assigned to joystick button 2.

CONFIG_PC1640_NVR_MOUSE1_TOKEN
  Default Amstrad PC1640 NVR token assigned to mouse button 1.

CONFIG_PC1640_NVR_MOUSE2_TOKEN
  Default Amstrad PC1640 NVR token assigned to mouse button 2.

CONFIG_PC1640_NVR_MOUSE_X_SCALE
  Default Amstrad PC1640 NVR mouse X scale byte (0-255).

CONFIG_PC1640_NVR_MOUSE_Y_SCALE
  Default Amstrad PC1640 NVR mouse Y scale byte (0-255).

CONFIG_PC1640_NVR_RAMDISK_SIZE
  Default Amstrad PC1640 NVR RAM disk size byte.

CONFIG_POST_PRETTY_WAIT_PANEL
  Show a formatted POST progress panel during boot.

CONFIG_POST_SPACE_INVADERS_SOUND
  Play a Space Invaders-style sound effect through the speaker
  during cold boot POST.

CONFIG_DEBUG_PORT_E9
  Route debug output to I/O port 0xE9 (Bochs/QEMU debug console).

CONFIG_DEBUG_COM1
  Route debug output to the COM1 serial port.

CONFIG_DEBUG_VIDEO_STATE
  Enable verbose tracing of video state changes.

CONFIG_DEBUG_VIDEO_OVERLAY
  Enable video debug overlay display.

CONFIG_TRACE_VIDEO_COM1
  Mirror video trace output to COM1.

FDC_BOOT_TRACE (Makefile only, not Kconfig)
  Build with: make FDC_BOOT_TRACE=1
  Emits compact INT19 / FDC-read checkpoints to I/O port 0xE9. Use a debug
  build of the emulator if it logs that port, or correlate with FDC I/O in
  the VM log.  CONFIG_DEBUG_COM1 is not used here (full serial debug overflows
  the 16 KiB PC1640 ROM image).
